  "limitations": "This does not complete MR-10 or the 17-package goal. The new transport fixtures use mechanically withheld snapshot completions and do not qualify native physical snapshot RPCs, source/receiver transfer lifetime, automatic checkpoint scheduling or member repair. Native incoming snapshots/automatic compaction remain disabled; missing_quorum_restore_refused and authorized fresh-member S3/peer seeding remain unfinished. Snapshot-failure hints are soft Raft progress signals, never install/commit proof; native transfer leases must still bind exact source term/index/descriptor, cancellation, retry, expiry and current member/process authorization. Fixed completion and hint reservations supplement ordinary request limits; full operational watermarks remain MR-13. Materialized and empty/configuration snapshots and maximum-size archive restore are component-qualified; the 64-MiB fixture mechanically seeds a verified image and does not establish a 64-MiB SDK command envelope. Per-command envelope bounds are unchanged. Archive recovery uses the in-memory object-store adapter. Independent snapshot/current/private/apply generation admission still needs native integration. External Blob/effect dependency closure remains MR-12. Process kill and injected sync failure do not establish physical power-loss behavior. No physical S3, zones, production capacity/performance or full release qualification is claimed. Node qualification is the single affected public Raft lifecycle case; the earlier physical record pins its separate 88-case run. Seven ignored child entry points are invoked by owning parents and excluded. Existing vendored warnings remain visible.",
